            <ArticleTitle>Role of analgesic adjuncts in postoperative pain management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>85-107</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postoperative pain remains a major problem. A multi-modal analgesic approach is recommended to optimize pain management and reduce opiate-related adverse effects. Several analgesic adjuncts have been investigated, and many have proved to have a useful analgesic effect. This article reviews the literature regarding use of analgesic adjuncts in the perioperative period.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
